  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $109M in contracts in FY2027 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services issued 740 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $147K. Obligations fell 99.6% year over year compared with prior full fiscal years, reflecting that FY2027 totals are partial and cover only the fiscal year to date. Obligations by fiscal year show prior annual totals of $33.4B in FY22, $33.4B in FY23, $29.9B in FY24, $21.3B in FY25, and $24.9B in FY26. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the top spending category in FY2027 to date at $27.8M, followed by Custom Computer Programming Services at $17.2M and All Other Outpatient Care Centers at $12.3M. AMERICAN TYPE CULTURE COLLECTION is the top vendor in FY2027 to date at $23.5M, with PERATON INC. second at $18.7M. This snapshot captures current-year contract obligations only; full-year totals will change as the fiscal year progresses.",
    "sections": [
