        "heading": "How do FY2027 to date obligations compare with prior years?",
        "body": "The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $109M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services recorded $33.4B in FY22, $33.4B in FY23, $29.9B in FY24, $21.3B in FY25, and $24.9B in FY26. Obligations fell 99.6% year over year, reflecting that FY2027 totals are partial and cover only the fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the top categories and vendors in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the top category at $27.8M, followed by Custom Computer Programming Services at $17.2M and All Other Outpatient Care Centers at $12.3M. AMERICAN TYPE CULTURE COLLECTION is the largest vendor at $23.5M, followed by PERATON INC. at $18.7M and CAS FSE JV II LLC at $8.9M."
