  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Health and Human Services spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $109M in contracts in FY2027 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services issued 740 awards so far this fiscal year with an average award size of $147K. Obligations fell 99.6% year over year, and prior full-year totals were $33.4B in FY22, $33.4B in FY23, $29.9B in FY24, $21.3B in FY25, and $24.9B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Health and Human Services buy?",
      "a": "Health and Human Services buys research, IT, clinical, and support services. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the largest FY2027 to date category at $27.8M, Custom Computer Programming Services is $17.2M, All Other Outpatient Care Centers is $12.3M, Facilities Support Services is $10.3M, and Other Computer Related Services is $10M. Additional categories in the top 10 include Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $7.7M and Research and Development in Biotechnology at $6.9M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Health and Human Services's largest contractors?",
      "a": "AMERICAN TYPE CULTURE COLLECTION is the largest contractor at $23.5M. PERATON INC. is the second-largest contractor at $18.7M, CAS FSE JV II LLC is $8.9M, AXLE INFORMATICS, LLC is $7.5M, and LOCUS BIOSCIENCES INC is $5.3M. The FY2027 to date top 10 also includes GUIDEHOUSE INC. at $4.7M and FIRST NATIONS COMMUNITY HEALTH SOURCE INC at $3.6M."
